From 422b49bcf01af2a0e1c59b028c63e98ca181e5f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 15:49:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rga-rewrite: add RGA userptr-IOMMU userptr mapping

The compatibility rewrite pinned userptr pages, called dma_map_sgtable(),
and then programmed only the first returned DMA address. That matches the
vendor ABI only when the DMA API gives RGA one non-wrapping span;
fragmented userptrs can otherwise fault RGA3.

Share the forward-port RGA userptr-IOMMU design in the rewrite: validate dma-buf
imports fail-closed, but for pinned userptr sg-tables fall back to a
driver-owned contiguous IOVA allocation in the translated RGA domain and
map a page-aligned sg-table copy with iommu_map_sg(). Clear the sg-table
DMA bookkeeping left by the abandoned DMA API map so later userptr cache
syncs use the physical pages, not stale SWIOTLB state. Fail closed if the
IOVA granule is larger than PAGE_SIZE, where padding could break RGA's
byte-contiguous view. Track RGA userptr-IOMMU ownership in both persistent imports
and per-job remaps so release tears down the right mapping. Harden the
32-bit span validator so arithmetic overflow fails closed.

Expose the DMA-API IOVA allocator through a small iommu-dma helper instead
of casting the private cookie through a rewrite-local shadow type.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/iommu/dma-iommu.c                     |  14 +
 .../video/rockchip/rga-rewrite/rga_rewrite.c  | 438 +++++++++++++++++-
 include/linux/iommu.h                         |   9 +
 3 files changed, 443 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/dma-iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/dma-iommu.c
index f1fb27681b0b..b470c181c03c 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/dma-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/dma-iommu.c
@@ -384,2 +384,16 @@ int iommu_get_dma_cookie(struct iommu_domain *domain)
 
+/**
+ * iommu_dma_get_iova_domain - Return the DMA-API IOVA allocator for a domain
+ * @domain: IOMMU domain prepared for DMA-API usage
+ */
+struct iova_domain *iommu_dma_get_iova_domain(struct iommu_domain *domain)
+{
+	if (!domain || domain->cookie_type != IOMMU_COOKIE_DMA_IOVA ||
+	    !domain->iova_cookie)
+		return NULL;
+
+	return &domain->iova_cookie->iovad;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(iommu_dma_get_iova_domain);
+
 /**
